#: cinatra.php:4966
msgid "This database session ends transactions with a chain or a disconnect ( completion_type is not NO_CHAIN ), so the ability could not prove that no transaction is open after its own. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:4968
msgid "A database transaction is already open on this connection ( or the call came from inside this ability's own save ), and starting another would commit it. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5180
msgid "The database did not report whether a transaction is already open on this connection, so the write cannot be made safely. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5210
msgid "The site's object cache still serves a copy of the post that differs from the database ( site code cached it during the save, and the cache did not accept its removal ); WordPress may show that copy until the cache entry is replaced or expires."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5245
msgid "The posts table does not use the InnoDB storage engine, so the post cannot be locked during the check. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5279
msgid "This ability writes only published posts and drafts. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5294
msgid "Another user is editing this post right now. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5320
msgid "The post changed since it was read. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5386
msgid "The post would be empty ( content, title and excerpt ), or a site policy considers it empty. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5399
msgid "A site save policy for the post status does not allow this save. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5442
msgid "A site save policy ( wp_insert_post_data ) would change parts of the post this ability does not write. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5472
msgid "The posts table has a column name this ability cannot compare safely. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5487
msgid "The database update failed. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5492
msgid "The post could not be read back after the update. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5501
msgid "The conditional write matched no row although the post reads unchanged. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5507
msgid "Site code changed the post row during the save, so the conditional write matched no row. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5525
msgid "The post row after the write is not exactly what this save wrote ( site code changed it during the save ). Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5585
msgid "The database transaction could not be marked. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5591
msgid "The database does not report this session's statement counters ( SHOW SESSION STATUS ), which the write needs to prove that it owns its transaction. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5599
msgid "The database transaction could not be started. Nothing was written."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5696
msgid "This ability could not prove that its database transaction stayed its own through the end of the save, and the post could not be read back, so it is not known whether the change was stored. Site code that ran during the save may also have stored changes. Read the post before trying again."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5699
msgid "This ability could not prove that its database transaction stayed its own through the end of the save. The post now holds exactly the change this save intended, but that does not prove this save stored it ( another save can store the same values ), so the site's after-save hooks were not run for it. Site code that ran during the save may also have stored changes. Read the post before trying again."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5702
msgid "This ability could not prove that its database transaction stayed its own through the end of the save, and the post read back is not exactly the change this save intended, so it is not known what was stored ( a post that reads as before the save does not prove that nothing was written ). Site code that ran during the save may also have stored changes. Read the post before trying again."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5780
msgid "Refusal code, present only when success is false."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5799
msgid "On a successful write: true when the site's object cache did not accept the invalidation after the commit, so get_post() may still return the post as it was before this save. On a refusal: true when the cache still serves a copy that differs from the database after the rollback."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5803
msgid "On write_outcome_unknown ( always true ): the ability could not show that its transaction stayed its own, so changes that site code stored during the save may remain."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5819
msgid "SHA-256 fingerprint of every column of the posts row as read ( meta and terms are outside it ). Send it back as expected.row_token."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5826
msgid "Written fields whose stored value differs from the sent value because the save filters changed it."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5856
msgid "Cinatra abilities for reading a post and writing a reviewed change to it."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5877
msgid "The numeric ID of the post or page."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5884
msgid "Read a post for review"
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5885
msgid "Read the raw stored title, content, excerpt, status, type, permalink and post_modified_gmt of a post or page, fresh from the database. Pass post_modified_gmt to cinatra/post-update-if-unchanged as if_unmodified_since."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5913
msgid "Write a reviewed change to a post"
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5914
msgid "Write title, content and/or excerpt of a published post or draft (and optionally move it to draft) only if the post is unchanged since the read the review was based on. Writes only those columns. Refuses with a code (for example post_changed, post_locked, unsupported_status or invalid) and then writes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5923
msgid "The post_modified_gmt value of the read the change is based on."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5935
msgid "The row_token returned by cinatra/post-read for the read the change is based on."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5940
msgid "The title, content, excerpt and status as read, byte for byte, and the row_token of that read; always all five."
msgstr ""

#: cinatra.php:5948
msgid "Only \"draft\": move the post to draft in the same save. Omit to keep the current status."
msgstr ""
